  "instructions": "## How to Use This Collection\n\n1. **Set Base URL**: Update `base_url` variable to your API server (default: http://localhost:8000)\n\n2. **Setup Variables**:\n   - Run \"Login - Valid Credentials\" first\n   - Extract token from response (if using token auth)\n   - Set `token` variable\n\n3. **Critical Tests**:\n   - Focus on CRITICAL tests first (marked with 🔴)\n   - These validate business rules that MUST work\n\n4. **Run in Order**:\n   - Authentication tests first\n   - Book CRUD tests\n   - Movement tests (especially critical ones)\n\n5. **Expected Failures**:\n   - 404 errors indicate routes not yet implemented (OK for now)\n   - 422 errors indicate validation failures (expected for invalid input)\n   - 200/201 indicate success\n\n## Critical Success Criteria\n\n✅ Saida blocks when quantity > stock → HTTP 422\n✅ Saida requires justification → HTTP 422 if missing\n✅ Stock never goes negative → Always >= 0\n✅ Entrada always works → Never fails with valid data\n✅ ISBN must be unique → 422 on duplicate\n"
